    "Development resource/throughput evidence on eight fresh original unlabelled 50–71-byte inputs; no semantic accuracy, generalization, production SLA or real Riido LLM savings evidence.",
    "Three short fixed runs only; repeats have different duration/call budgets per arm, a shared live server and possible concurrent host activity. Quantiles are per-run and summarized across repeats, not pooled.",
    "Predict latency brackets the Go call; whole-loop throughput includes timers, checksums, deterministic-output checks and loop work. HTTP latency includes request construction, loopback transport, server work, response read/JSON decode and pin validation. No isolated network overhead estimate.",
    "External maximum RSS covers the measured process: in-process helper, or HTTP client helper only. HTTP helper also verifies/loads a duplicate local model and retains instrumentation; already-running server RSS/CPU are not measured. RSS includes more than Go heap.",
    "Go MemStats measures Go-managed allocations and memory; latency sample arrays and bookkeeping are included in retained heap. It does not report native/GPU memory. CGO was disabled and no GPU inference was needed.",
    "Each direct loop recorded 16 bytes/one timed allocation overall; this is near-zero observed per-call allocation, not a claim that Predict alone allocates exactly zero.",
    "Server inference_us is integer microseconds from the live response. Raw JSON reused *_ns subfield names inside server_inference_reported_us; aggregate normalizes these to *_us without altering numerical observations.",
    "External time CPU/wall fields are rounded to 0.01 seconds and include startup, model hash/load, warmup, GC and output; the first direct process had additional startup wall time. No whole-host CPU utilization estimate.",
    "Eight original unlabelled probe phrases and the byte-exact measured helper are now public exposed development material, excluded from future protected final datasets and selector tuning. Model artifacts/raw local logs remain private. No protected research data was read; no training, threshold/model selection, server restart or application writes occurred."
